            "lookup_key": "blog_remote_work_body",
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<p>Remote teams do not fail because people are far apart. They fail because expectations live in someone's head instead of in writing.</p><h3>Write things down</h3><p>Every decision that matters gets a short written summary: what we chose, what we rejected, and who owns the next step.</p><h3>Default to async</h3><p>Meetings are the most expensive way to share information. Use them for debate and decisions, not status updates.</p><h3>Protect deep work</h3><p>Block long, uninterrupted stretches on the shared calendar and treat them as real commitments.</p>",
